    "reason": "A bone toggle's resting side is read off the pose rather than off the member declared beside it. A toggle names the state a subject is not resting in, and what it rests in is something the model already says - a goat draws its horns because hasLeftHorn is what a goat's render state is built holding. The derived answer matches the shipped member for every toggle but the bee's, which is the two having drifted: BeeRenderState builds hasStinger at one, so a bee rests with its sting and the member said otherwise. Only the dump moves, in the bone_toggles it records; every sweep, every pin and manifest.visual held their row counts and their sums, no rendered byte having changed.",
